  title: 'Acceptance and Commitment Therapy: Core Processes for Clinicians',
  slug: SLUG,
  description: 'This course provides licensed mental health clinicians with a comprehensive grounding in Acceptance and Commitment Therapy (ACT). Participants will explore the theoretical foundations of ACT within the contextual behavioral science framework, learn to work with all six core processes of the ACT Hexaflex, apply ACT techniques with diverse clinical presentations, and understand how to adapt ACT principles for culturally responsive practice.',
